# Version Commit Convention

When writing commit messages that will trigger a build, include one of these keywords to control the version bump. CI reads the commit message and bumps `app.json` accordingly.

## Keywords (case-insensitive)

| Keyword | Result |
|---------|--------|
| `major`, `major release`, `[major]`, `(major)` | 1.0.1 → **2.0.0** |
| `version upgrade`, `[minor]`, `(minor)` | 1.0.1 → **1.1.0** |
| `patch`, `[patch]`, `(patch)` | 1.0.1 → **1.0.2** |
| *(default)* | 1.0.1 → **1.0.2** |

## Examples

```
fix: resolve crash [patch]
feat: add dark mode - Version upgrade
BREAKING: New API - Major release
```

First matching keyword wins (major > minor > patch).
